<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luna Vasahi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1230</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Luna Vasahi is a white marble Jain temple dedicated to Neminatha in the Dilwara temple complex at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It was built in 1230 by the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tejapala">Tejapala</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastupala">Vastupala</a>, in memory of his son Lunasimha. Its ceilings and pillars are carved with extremely delicate marble ornament, and with the older <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimal-shah">Vimala</a> Vasahi it is among the masterpieces of Jain architecture.</p></div>
